{
  "version": 2,
  "comment": "Cross-language event contract. Java AiEventContractTest and web aiEvents.contract.test.ts both read THIS file. Adding, renaming or removing an event type or field must be reflected here and on both sides.",
  "entryShape": "Every entry of live[] and timeline[] is {type, example, exampleMinimal, absent}. `example` is the richest legal wire form: it populates every field of the type except the ones that cannot legitimately appear together with it (a successful tool_done carries no error). `absent` lists the OPTIONAL fields, i.e. the ones @JsonInclude(NON_NULL) drops when the server has nothing to say, so the client must tolerate their absence. `exampleMinimal` is the leanest legal wire form and therefore carries exactly the REQUIRED fields; for a type with no optional field it doubles as a second example that widens value coverage, which is how notice reaches level=error, run_status reaches a COMPLETED run with no reason, and the tool pair reaches a no-argument call whose input is {} instead of null. Both suites assert the two closure rules that make the entry self-checking: fields(type) == keys(example) U absent, and keys(exampleMinimal) == fields(type) \\ absent. Version 2 added exampleMinimal and absent; version 1 carried {type, example} only.",
